atted with `dependents.changelog( { package, source } )`:"],[986,"The bundle changelog entry defaults to `Bundle <source> <version>.` and is formatted with `dependents.changelog( { package, source } )`:"],[1408,"The bundle changelog entry defaults to `Bundle <source> <version>.` and is formatted with `dependents.changelog( { package, source } )`:"],[1830,"The bundle changelog entry defaults to `Bundle <source> <version>.` and is formatted with `dependents.changelog( { package, source } )`:"],[2295,"The canonical configuration is a workspace with package groups; a single-project config is one group covering the repository root:"],[2481,"The canonical configuration is a workspace with package groups; a single-project config is one group covering the repository root:"],[94,"The changeset commands manage versioning, changelogs and release tags for single-package repositories and monorepos, including this repository. They read Changesets-style Markdown and load JavaScript configs with descriptors for npm and Composer manifests, plugin and theme headers, readme Stable tags, PHP constants, and Git tags. Use JavaScript configs with ESM (`export default`) or CommonJS (`module.exports`). Frontmatter uses `package-name: patch|minor|major` entries. For pre-releases, use the built-in pre-release workflow; the parser supports this simple frontmatter format rather than general YAML or the Changesets pre mode."],[516,"The changeset commands manage versioning, changelogs and release tags for single-package repositories and monorepos, including this repository. They read Changesets-style Markdown and load JavaScript configs with descriptors for npm and Composer manifests, plugin and theme headers, readme Stable tags, PHP constants, and Git tags. Use JavaScript configs with ESM (`export default`) or CommonJS (`module.exports`). Frontmatter uses `package-name: patch|minor|major` entries. For pre-releases, use the built-in pre-release workflow; the parser supports this simple frontmatter format rather than general YAML or the Changesets pre mode."],[936,"The changeset commands manage versioning, changelogs and release tags for single-package repositories and monorepos, including this repository. They read Changesets-style Markdown and load JavaScript configs with descriptors for npm and Composer manifests, plugin and theme headers, readme Stable tags, PHP constants, and Git tags. Use JavaScript configs with ESM (`export default`) or CommonJS (`module.exports`). Frontmatter uses `package-name: patch|minor|major` entries. For pre-releases, use the built-in pre-release workflow; the parser supports this simple frontmatter format rather than general YAML or the Changesets pre mode."],[1358,"The changeset commands manage versioning, changelogs and release tags for single-package repositories and monorepos, including this repository. They read Changesets-style Markdown and load JavaScript configs with descriptors for npm and Composer manifests, plugin and theme headers, readme Stable tags, PHP constants, and Git tags. Use JavaScript configs with ESM (`export default`) or CommonJS (`module.exports`). Frontmatter uses `package-name: patch|minor|major` entries. For pre-releases, use the built-in pre-release workflow; the parser supports this simple frontmatter format rather than general YAML or the Changesets pre mode."],[1780,"The changeset commands manage versioning, changelogs and release tags for single-package repositories and monorepos, including this repository. They read Changesets-style Markdown and load JavaScript configs with descriptors for npm and Composer manifests, plugin and theme headers, readme Stable tags, PHP constants, and Git tags. Use JavaScript configs with ESM (`export default`) or CommonJS (`module.exports`). Frontmatter uses `package-name: patch|minor|major` entries. For pre-releases, use the built-in pre-release workflow; the parser supports this simple frontmatter format rather than general YAML or the Changesets pre mode."],[335,"The changeset release modules, from the entry point down:"],[757,"The changeset release modules, from the entry point down:"],[1177,"The changeset release modules, from the entry point down:"],[1599,"The changeset release modules, from the entry point down:"],[2021,"The changeset release modules, from the entry point down:"],[2224,"The CLI does not commit or publish, and only `tag` creates and, with `--push`, pushes tags. Review and commit version and changelog changes separately. A second `version` run with no pending changesets makes no release edits."],[2410,"The CLI does not commit or publish, and only `tag` creates and, with `--push`, pushes tags. Review and commit version and changelog changes separately. A second `version` run with no pending changesets makes no release edits."],[86,"The CLI is `chop [--data <dir>] [--port <n>] [--host <address>] [--scheme <name>] [--help]`, with flags overriding `CHOP_*` variables. Exit codes are `0`, `1` for a failure and `2` for invalid options. `SIGINT` and `SIGTERM` stop it gracefully, and `CHOP_ACCESS_LOG=1` prints one JSON line per request (R-CLI-1 to R-CLI-4)."],[2360,"The CLI prepares releases, and other actions publish them. These workflows check that pull requests add changesets, open a release pull request whenever changesets are pending on `main`, and after it's merged, create the tag and GitHub release of every released package. Packagist picks up the new tags of Composer packages; add the WP Release Zip and WP Release Deploy SVN actions to the `release` job to ship a WordPress plugin."],[2546,"The CLI prepares releases, and other actions publish them. These workflows check that pull requests add changesets, open a release pull request whenever changesets are pending on `main`, and after it's merged, create the tag and GitHub release of every released package. Packagist picks up the new tags of Composer packages; add the WP Release Zip and WP Release Deploy SVN actions to the `release` job to ship a WordPress plugin."],[2270,"The command is `changeset` with subcommands, like `changeset add`, where `wp-release` has `changeset-add` among its other commands. Run `changeset --help` for the commands."],[2456,"The command is `changeset` with subcommands, like `changeset add`, where `wp-release` has `changeset-add` among its other commands. Run `changeset --help` for the commands."],[257,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[679,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[1099,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md` when there's no `readme.txt`."],[1521,"The commands read the same headers as WordPress. The main plugin file is the top-level `.php` file with a `Plugin Name:` header in its first 8 KB, preferring `{slug}.php` when several files have one. A directory without a plugin file and with `Theme Name:` in `style.css` is a theme. The readme headers (`Stable tag`, `Tested up to`, …) come from `readme.txt`, or `readme.md